\fs32\b Preply Frontend to Vercel Deployment Guide\b0\fs22\par
\i Generated from the current Preply repository structure and configuration.\i0\par\par
\fs28\b 1. Project Overview\b0\fs22\par
Preply is an AI-powered interview preparation platform. Users register, upload a resume, choose interview settings, receive AI-generated questions, answer by typing or browser speech recognition, submit answers for AI evaluation, and view performance reports.\par\par
The repository contains three independent services:\par
- frontend: React single-page application\par
- backend: Node.js and Express REST API\par
- ai-service: Python FastAPI service using Google Gemini\par\par
\fs28\b 2. Technology Stack\b0\fs22\par
\b Frontend\b0\par
React 19, JavaScript/JSX, custom esbuild bundling, Tailwind CSS 4, React Router, Lucide React icons, Motion animations, and pdfjs-dist. It is not Vite, Next.js, Angular, TypeScript, or Create React App.\par\par
\b Backend\b0\par
Node.js, Express 4, ES modules, Mongoose, bcryptjs, jsonwebtoken, cors, and nodemon.\par\par
\b AI service\b0\par
Python, FastAPI, Uvicorn, Pydantic, httpx, python-dotenv, and Google GenAI.\par\par
\b Database\b0\par
MongoDB accessed through Mongoose. Production should use MongoDB Atlas or another publicly reachable MongoDB deployment.\par\par
\b Authentication\b0\par
Passwords are hashed with bcryptjs. Login returns a JWT. The frontend stores the token in localStorage under preply_token and sends it as an Authorization Bearer header. Authentication is not cookie-based.\par\par
