\b Important files\b0\par
frontend/src/services/api.js centralizes all frontend API calls and reads REACT_APP_API_URL. frontend/src/routes/AppRoutes.jsx defines React Router routes. backend/src/app.js configures Express, CORS, middleware, and REST routes. backend/src/config/env.js loads backend variables. ai-service/app.py exposes the FastAPI AI endpoints.\par\par
\fs28\b 4. API Communication\b0\fs22\par
The frontend calls the backend through REST endpoints under /api:\par
- POST /api/auth/register\par
- POST /api/auth/login\par
- GET /api/auth/me\par
- POST /api/interviews\par
- GET /api/interviews\par
- GET /api/interviews/:id\par
- POST /api/interviews/:id/answer\par
- GET /api/interviews/:id/report\par
- GET /api/reports/today\par
- GET /api/reports/history\par
- GET /api/health\par\par
The backend calls the AI service through:\par
- POST /api/resume/parse\par
- POST /api/interview/generate-question\par
- POST /api/interview/evaluate-answer\par
- POST /api/interview/generate-report\par\par
The browser never calls MongoDB, Gemini, or the AI service directly.\par\par
\fs28\b 5. Environment Variables\b0\fs22\par
\b Frontend: frontend/.env\b0\par
REACT_APP_API_URL=http://localhost:5000\par
PORT=3000\par\par
For Vercel, set only:\par
REACT_APP_API_URL=https://your-public-backend.example.com\par\par
REACT_APP_API_URL is safe to expose because it is only a public API address. It is compiled into browser JavaScript. The project requires the REACT_APP_ prefix; VITE_ and NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables will not work.\par\par
\b Backend: backend/.env\b0\par
PORT=5000\par
NODE_ENV=production\par
MONGODB_URI=<MongoDB Atlas connection string>\par
JWT_SECRET=<strong private random secret>\par
AI_SERVICE_URL=https://your-public-ai-service.example.com\par
FRONTEND_URL=https://your-project.vercel.app\par\par
\b AI service: ai-service/.env\b0\par
PORT=8000\par
GEMINI_API_KEY=<private Gemini API key>\par
GEMINI_MODEL=<supported Gemini model>\par\par
Never place MONGODB_URI, JWT_SECRET, GEMINI_API_KEY, or private tokens in Vercel frontend variables.\par\par
\fs28\b 6. Localhost and Production Problems\b0\fs22\par
The frontend fallback in frontend/src/services/api.js is http://localhost:5000. This is only for local development. The Vercel variable REACT_APP_API_URL must override it with the public backend URL.\par\par
Backend local defaults include localhost:3000, localhost:5000, localhost:8000, and 127.0.0.1:8000. Replace them through backend and AI-service production environment variables. A deployed browser cannot reach localhost on your computer.\par\par
\fs28\b 7. Vercel Configuration\b0\fs22\par
Deploy the frontend subdirectory, not the repository root.\par\par
Root Directory: frontend\par
Framework Preset: Other\par
Install Command: npm ci\par
Build Command: npm run build\par
Output Directory: build\par
Node.js: 20.x or newer\par
Vercel environment variable: REACT_APP_API_URL\par\par
The custom frontend build script uses esbuild and Tailwind CLI and creates frontend/build. Do not use npm start as the Vercel build command.\par\par
Because the app uses BrowserRouter, add frontend/vercel.json with this content to support direct refreshes of routes such as /dashboard and /profile:\par
\f1\fs20
{\par
  "rewrites": [\par
    {\par
      "source": "/(.*)",\par
      "destination": "/index.html"\par
    }\par
  ]\par
}\par
\f0\fs22\par
\fs28\b 8. Backend Deployment Dependency\b0\fs22\par
The backend is currently a local Node/Express service on port 5000. It must be deployed separately to Render, Railway, Fly.io, Azure, AWS, or another Node.js host. The AI service must also be deployed separately. MongoDB must be hosted by MongoDB Atlas or another accessible provider.\par\par
Configure the backend with:\par
NODE_ENV=production\par
MONGODB_URI=<production MongoDB connection string>\par
JWT_SECRET=<private secret>\par
AI_SERVICE_URL=https://your-ai-service.example.com\par
FRONTEND_URL=https://your-project.vercel.app\par\par
The backend already supports CORS configuration through FRONTEND_URL. The Vercel origin must match exactly. Since authentication uses Authorization headers and localStorage, cross-domain cookies are not required. HTTPS should be used for the frontend, backend, and AI service.\par\par
\fs28\b 9. Deployment Procedure\b0\fs22\par
\b Step 1: Install and test locally\b0\par
Open a terminal in the repository and run:\par
\f1\fs20
cd frontend\par
npm ci\par
npm start\par
\f0\fs22
Open http://localhost:3000. The React home page should load.\par\par
\b Step 2: Build locally\b0\par
Run:\par
\f1\fs20
npm run build\par
\f0\fs22
The command should generate frontend/build without errors.\par\par
\b Step 3: Deploy the backend and AI service\b0\par
Deploy backend and ai-service separately. Verify:\par
https://your-backend.example.com/api/health\par
https://your-ai-service.example.com/health\par
The backend health endpoint should report a connected database.\par\par
\b Step 4: Push to GitHub\b0\par
Commit the source and package-lock files. Do not commit .env files.\par\par
\b Step 5: Create the Vercel project\b0\par
In Vercel, click Add New, Project, and import the GitHub repository. Set Root Directory to frontend.\par\par
\b Step 6: Configure build settings\b0\par
Set Framework Preset to Other, Install Command to npm ci, Build Command to npm run build, and Output Directory to build.\par\par
\b Step 7: Add the environment variable\b0\par
In Project Settings > Environment Variables, add REACT_APP_API_URL with the public HTTPS backend URL. Enable it for Production and Preview.\par\par
\b Step 8: Deploy and test\b0\par
Click Deploy. Test the home page, login, registration, dashboard, interview setup, reports, profile, and direct refreshes of nested routes.\par\par
\b Step 9: Diagnose errors\b0\par
If the build fails, confirm Root Directory is frontend and Output Directory is build. If API requests use localhost, check REACT_APP_API_URL and redeploy. If requests fail with CORS, set backend FRONTEND_URL to the exact Vercel origin and redeploy the backend. If nested routes return 404, add vercel.json and redeploy.\par\par
